window.OSAP_FT=window.OSAP_FT||{};window.OSAP_FT["39"]={"https://theconversation.com/how-political-disagreement-with-our-neighbours-relates-to-whether-we-bother-casting-a-ballot-295642":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T16:30Z","sha":"e6a9e7bf8334e9a85daa16d5ca823cb4ac22d6299f779475f170cbfe38368619","read":"https://theconversation.com/how-political-disagreement-with-our-neighbours-relates-to-whether-we-bother-casting-a-ballot-295642","bytes":183813,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"How political disagreement with our neighbours relates to whether we bother casting a ballot","by":[{"n":"Md Mujahedul Islam","r":"SSHRC Postdoctoral Fellow, Department of Government, Cornell University"}],"pub":"2026-11-02T17:28:40Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["In the 2025 federal election, Canadians voted at ",["the highest rate since 1993","https://www.elections.ca/res/rec/eval/pes2025/evt/evt_e.pdf"],". Explanations for high or low turnout usually focus on the national election campaign, including how close the race was and what seemed to be at stake."]},{"k":"p","s":["As lead author of a ",["new study published in the Canadian Journal of Political Science","https://doi.org/10.1017/S0008423926101462"],", I worked with my co-authors — Daniel Rubenson, Roosmarijn de Geus, Benjamin Allen Stevens and Peter John Loewen — to look close to home and examine how someone’s political views compare with those of the people around them."]},{"k":"p","s":["Our research shows that people whose views closely match the average views in their riding are less likely to vote than those whose views differ moderately. Similarly, people whose views differ extensively from those around them are less likely to vote. In short, voting peaks at moderate levels of disagreement."]},{"k":"h","s":["Measuring disagreement next door"]},{"k":"p","s":["We used the ",["Local Parliament Project","https://doi.org/10.7910/DVN/DACHKP"],", an online survey of more than 31,000 Canadians conducted during the 2015 federal election campaign, in our research. It included respondents from nearly every riding, which allowed us to compare each person’s views with those of others in the same riding."]},{"k":"p","s":["Research shows labels like “left” and “right” ",["mean different things to different people","https://doi.org/10.1007/s11109-016-9368-2"],". We, therefore, measured political views using people’s positions on 37 specific issues, such as taxes, health care and immigration."]},{"k":"p","s":["This allowed us to see how far each person’s views were from their neighbours’ in the same riding, and the diversity of opinions across the riding as a whole. This captured different information. For example, a riding’s voters can be largely like-minded, yet some people living there can still hold differing views about specific issues."]},{"k":"h","s":["A sweet spot for voting"]},{"k":"p","s":["We found that a person whose views are very similar to their riding’s average has a predicted 83 per cent chance of voting. A person at the opposite extreme has a predicted 63 per cent chance, though this estimate is less precise. People halfway between these extremes have the highest likelihood of voting, at 90 per cent."]},{"k":"p","s":["These patterns hold after we account for factors that include age, education, income, how close the local race was and how much parties campaigned. Ridings with tight races in 2015 did not have higher turnout than those where one party won easily."]},{"k":"p","s":["Our riding-level analysis shows a similar picture. Predicted turnout is 65.7 per cent at the lowest level of opinion diversity, rises to 68.7 per cent at the mid-point and falls to 65.3 per cent at the highest. However, these differences are not statistically significant once we account for other factors."]},{"k":"p","s":["The link between a person’s views and voting also varies with the local mix of views. In ridings with a wide range of views, voting peaks at smaller differences and drops off more steeply for people whose views differ extensively."]},{"k":"p","s":["So two people equally far from how most of their neighbours intend to vote can have different chances of showing up to cast a ballot depending on their riding."]},{"k":"h","s":["Disagreement can boost voter turnout"]},{"k":"p","s":["When our views match those around us, we rarely hear disagreement. Politics can feel settled, and our vote may seem unnecessary. Some disagreement changes that. It makes political differences more visible and the choice on the ballot feel more important."]},{"k":"p","s":["But too much disagreement can do the opposite. When we’re surrounded by very different views, the competing signals can make politics confusing and overwhelming. This can also feel socially uncomfortable."]},{"k":"p","s":["Earlier research has found that people in ",["highly conflict-ridden social networks","https://doi.org/10.1017/S0003055402004264"]," sometimes pull back from politics to avoid straining relationships with friends, family and co-workers."]},{"k":"h","s":["What this means for Canada"]},{"k":"p","s":["Our data come from 2015, when Liberal Justin Trudeau ended up winning a majority government, but the campaign was ",["a tight three-way race for much of its run","https://www.utoronto.ca/news/election-2015-polling-despite-marked-increase-support-ndp-its-still-three-way-race-expert-says"],". There was a wide range of views across ridings, making it a suitable election for studying how disagreement relates to voting."]},{"k":"p","s":["We think the same forces are likely at work in later elections, including 2025. So how voters experience disagreement in their own communities may matter for turnout, not just how close the race is."]},{"k":"p","s":["The findings also matter when riding maps change. When boundaries are redrawn, like they were in Québec in ",["39 provincial ridings","https://www.electionsquebec.qc.ca/en/electoral-maps/review-of-quebecs-electoral-map/electoral-map-final-boundaries/"]," ahead of its recent election, the mix of neighbours who voters live among shifts too."]},{"k":"p","s":["Our study also adds to the debate about political division. Research on Canadian voting habits has focused on ",["how warmly or coldly people feel toward the other side","https://theconversation.com/canada-isnt-deeply-polarized-yet-what-new-research-reveals-about-partisan-animosity-267719"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["Canada isn’t deeply polarized — yet. What new research reveals about partisan animosity","https://theconversation.com/canada-isnt-deeply-polarized-yet-what-new-research-reveals-about-partisan-animosity-267719"]]},{"k":"p","s":["Our results raise a different concern. People whose views closely mirror those around them are somewhat less likely to vote than those whose views differ moderately."]},{"k":"p","s":["Our study has a clear scope. It covers one election in a system where the candidate with the most votes wins each riding. Our survey results rely on stated intentions to vote, and show an association between how much people’s views differ from those around them and voter turnout. The next test is whether these findings held in 2025."]},{"k":"p","s":["The lesson, however, is worth taking seriously. A healthy democracy may depend not on eliminating political disagreement, but on keeping it within a range people can engage with."]}],"chars":5359},"https://theconversation.com/slapps-ndas-and-gendered-lawfare-how-the-rich-and-powerful-silence-victims-of-sexual-offences-296520":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T16:38Z","sha":"6fbcd0d7aa52703bfd967d2af2f2169246e6707987b68ed4a3c91f3c195fcd1e","read":"https://theconversation.com/slapps-ndas-and-gendered-lawfare-how-the-rich-and-powerful-silence-victims-of-sexual-offences-296520","bytes":182065,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Slapps, NDAs and gendered ‘lawfare’: how the rich and powerful silence victims of sexual offences","by":[{"n":"Francesca Farrington","r":"Lecturer in Law, School of Law and Social Justice, University of Liverpool"}],"pub":"2026-11-12T18:36:27Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["The conviction of Russell Brand came nearly two decades after “Me Too” was coined. Yet the years the former comedian avoided accountability serve as a stark reminder of the dangers victims still face when speaking out. The truth is that women who name predators are increasingly at risk of legal proceedings."]},{"k":"p","s":["While the ",["#MeToo","https://theconversation.com/topics/metoo-45316"]," movement emboldened victims to speak truth to power, it also exposed the tactics offenders use to silence them. UN special rapporteur ",["Irene Khan","https://docs.un.org/en/A/76/258"],", described this as a “perverse twist” in the age of #MeToo."]},{"k":"p","s":[["Research","https://papers.ssrn.com/sol3/papers.cfm?abstract_id=6958538"]," has shed light on what’s really happening here – mechanisms designed to provide justice can be used to suppress victims and provide impunity for those with money and power. So how can this happen in countries that are supposed to be committed to fundamental rights and the rule of law?"]},{"k":"p","s":["Across the world, powerful people are evading scrutiny by threatening legal action that could leave their accusers ruined financially. When powerful people use the law, or even just the threat of it, to suppress criticism, it is known as strategic lawsuits against public participation (Slapp)."]},{"k":"p","s":["You might wonder why courts don’t simply dismiss these cases. In practice, it is rare that they even ",["make it before a judge","https://antislapp.uk/2025/10/16/nina-cresswell-response-report/"],", because the threat is often enough to push a settlement. For many, as ",["one victim said","https://antislapp.uk/2025/10/16/nina-cresswell-response-report/"],", “silence is the only way to survive”. The aim is not to win the case, but to turn the process of defending the action into a punishment."]},{"k":"h","s":["Gendered lawfare"]},{"k":"p","s":["Slapps take many forms. ",["Many people","https://youth.europa.eu/young-journalists/articles/daphnes-law-honouring-legacy-of-fearless-journalist-fight-press-freedom_en"]," might picture a corporation or politician suing a public watchdog. Less well known are Slapps targeting victims of sexual and gender-based violence (SGBV). Often referred to as a kind of gendered censorship or gendered lawfare, these lawsuits ",["are prevalent","https://papers.ssrn.com/sol3/papers.cfm?abstract_id=6958538"]," and equally chilling. Rather than seeking justice, these legal tactics are used to create fear, financial pressure and a culture of self-censorship."]},{"k":"p","s":["When reporting on SGBV, the ",["stakes are high enough","https://www.theguardian.com/culture/2023/sep/24/russell-brand-and-why-the-allegations-took-so-long-to-surface"]," for large media organisations. So imagine how high they are for victims. In 2023, a woman called ",["Nina Cresswell","https://antislapp.uk/project/nina-cresswell/"]," shared her story of sexual abuse on social media. It related to an incident in 2010, and Cresswell said she was motivated to speak out by guilt at the thought of another woman suffering what she had gone through."]},{"k":"p","s":["But just days later, her alleged abuser sued her for defamation. The lawsuit did three things. By suing Cresswell, the perpetrator denied the abuse, attacked his accuser, and recast himself as the victim. This tactic is known as Darvo – Deny, Attack, Reverse Victim and Offender. It has become an ",["integral part","https://papers.ssrn.com/sol3/papers.cfm?abstract_id=6958538"]," of gendered-Slapp suits. Cresswell won her case, but she lost almost ",["three years of her life","https://antislapp.uk/2025/10/16/nina-cresswell-response-report/"]," to litigation. No police action was taken against the man."]},{"k":"p","s":[["Brand has been accused","https://www.latimes.com/entertainment-arts/story/2023-09-16/russell-brand-rape-sexual-assault-allegations-denial-video-times-channel-4?googsrc=ai-uk"]," of similar tactics. He reportedly obtained ",["an anti-harassment injunction","https://taxpolicy.org.uk/2026/11/07/russell-brand-secret-injunction/"]," against ",["Szilvia Berki","https://www.thetimes.com/uk/law/article/russell-brand-gagging-order-accuser-sx799n956"]," after she made allegations against him. The injunction – which is still in place – is far-reaching and prohibits Berki from repeating her allegations, including to friends and family."]},{"k":"p","s":["She was left with £50,000 in legal costs, and the judge authorised Brand’s lawyers to begin ",["bankruptcy proceedings","https://www.thetimes.com/uk/law/article/russell-brand-gagging-order-accuser-sx799n956"]," against her. While the full story behind the injunction appears to be complicated, Berki’s experience shows the scope of these gagging orders and the financial cost associated with fighting one."]},{"k":"p","s":["Entertainer ",["David Walliams","https://www.theguardian.com/media/2026/nov/10/david-walliams-allegations-high-court-case-key-legal-issues?googsrc=ai-uk"]," attempted to secure an injunction to suppress claims of sexual misconduct. While he denies all allegations against him, his application was refused and the findings of investigations by ",["The Guardian","https://www.theguardian.com/tv-and-radio/ng-interactive/2026/nov/10/david-walliams-accused-sex-grooming-allegations-young-women"]," and ",["ITV News","https://www.itv.com/news/2026-11-10/david-walliams-accused-of-preying-on-teenage-girls-as-young-as-15?googsrc=ai-uk"]," are now public."]},{"k":"p","s":["Non-disclosure agreements (NDAs) are also a major part of gendered censorship. For years, contracts were used to silence victims and witnesses of SGBV. ",["Zelda Perkins","https://www.theguardian.com/world/2025/jul/08/theres-nowhere-for-them-to-hide-any-more-zelda-perkins-on-harvey-weinstein-and-ndas"],", a former personal assistant to disgraced US film producer Harvey Weinstein, was bound by an NDA after she tried to expose his predatory behaviour."]},{"k":"p","s":["In a remarkable act of courage, she broke her NDA, exposing herself to substantial legal risk. She has been campaigning for reform ever since. On an episode of the ",["News Agents podcast","https://www.globalplayer.com/podcasts/episodes/7Ds3AeM/"],", Perkins revealed that she believes there are several women who entered into NDAs with Brand."]},{"k":"h","s":["Ending gendered censorship"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is no silver bullet in this struggle, yet there has been some progress. In the UK, the ",["Victims and Courts Act 2026","https://www.legislation.gov.uk/ukpga/2026/19/section/6"]," voids any provision in an agreement that prevents a disclosure relating to criminal conduct. And the ",["Employment Rights Act 2025","https://www.legislation.gov.uk/ukpga/2025/36/section/24"]," protects a worker’s right to disclose harassment and discrimination."]},{"k":"p","s":["But more must be done. ",["Perkins warned","https://www.globalplayer.com/podcasts/episodes/7Ds3AeM/"]," that Slapps – “the evil cousin of NDAs”, remain a real threat to victims. When it comes to combatting them, the UK lags behind other countries. In the UK, Slapp targets are only protected when reporting on ",["economic and financial crime","https://www.legislation.gov.uk/ukpga/2023/56/part/5/crossheading/power-to-strike-out-certain-claims/enacted"],", and even then, only to a ",["limited extent","https://www.birmingham.ac.uk/news/2025/new-mechanism-needed-in-english-law-to-slap-down-slapps-study"],". Victims of SGBV are left largely unprotected."]},{"k":"p","s":[["Parliament is debating","https://antislapp.uk/2026/06/16/two-private-members-bills-in-both-houses-place-anti-slapp-reform-firmly-on-the-parliamentary-agenda/"]," whether to extend protections to everyone speaking out on public interest matters. But recent reports have been a reminder that stronger anti-Slapp protections are needed to prevent the law becoming an instrument of the powerful against those alleging abuse."]}],"chars":5197},"https://theconversation.com/dari-tni-run-hingga-primarox-waspada-normalisasi-militerisme-di-panggung-olahraga-sipil-292782":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T16:47Z","sha":"0933fae4c323f086de0b38c43cf47f766bbae7b406e5c09118ce5b07e4fc8b3c","read":"https://theconversation.com/dari-tni-run-hingga-primarox-waspada-normalisasi-militerisme-di-panggung-olahraga-sipil-292782","bytes":181254,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Dari TNI Run hingga PRIMAROX: Waspada normalisasi militerisme di panggung olahraga sipil","by":[{"n":"Dini Dwi Kusumaningrum","r":"Peneliti, Badan Riset dan Inovasi Nasional (BRIN)"}],"pub":"2026-10-13T06:50:41Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["• Simbol militer dalam olahraga populer berpotensi menormalkan kehadiran militer di ruang sipil."]},{"k":"p","s":["• Kesetaraan di arena olahraga tidak menghapus ketimpangan kuasa antara militer dan warga sipil."]},{"k":"p","s":["• Keakraban dengan militer tidak boleh menggeser tuntutan akuntabilitas dan supremasi sipil."]},{"k":"p","s":["Lari, angkat beban, membalik ban raksasa, lalu mengunggah pencapaiannya ke media sosial sudah jadi bagian dari gaya hidup performatif masyarakat saat ini."]},{"k":"p","s":["Namun, bagaimana jika tantangan kebugaran itu menggunakan perlengkapan militer, lengkap dengan kehadiran tank dan kendaraan taktis di arena lomba?"]},{"k":"p","s":["Fenomena ini kian umum terlihat di berbagai event seperti ",["PRIMAROX Panglima TNI Cup 2026 di Indonesia Convention Exhibition (ICE) BSD, Kabupaten Tangerang","https://ice-indonesia.com/id/event/event_list/primarox-2026"],". Ada juga ",["TNI Run 2026 di Monas","https://megapolitan.antaranews.com/berita/550820/tni-run-2026-diikuti-ribuan-peserta-serta-sukses-catatkan-rekor-muri"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Berbagai event tersebut layaknya perhelatan ",["HYROX","https://www.instagram.com/p/Dck2f4LEgnm/"]," dan lari pada umumnya. Bedanya, ada sejumlah tantangan menggunakan ",["perlengkapan bernuansa militer","https://www.sandboxx.us/news/family-resources/health-and-wellness/keep-fit-on-deployment-with-these-improvised-workout-equipment-ideas/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Sebelum memasuki arena, pengunjung disambut pameran tank, kendaraan taktis TNI, dan café van yang menampilkan lirik Hymne Komando Kopassus TNI AD: “Lebih baik pulang nama daripada gagal dalam tugas”."]},{"k":"p","s":["Terpampang juga Ammo box carry yang mengharuskan peserta membawa kotak yang terinspirasi dari perlengkapan logistik militer. Sementara itu, tire flip menggunakan ban kendaraan taktis Anoa milik TNI dengan berat sekitar 84 kilogram. Corak militer juga hadir dalam desain jersey acara."]},{"k":"p","s":["Namun, di balik keseruan kompetisi, kita bisa bertanya: apa yang bisa terjadi ketika simbol militer semakin akrab dalam kehidupan sipil? Padahal, perluasan peran militer dalam demokrasi masih menjadi perdebatan."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["Selamat datang era ‘fitness-entertainment’: Bagaimana peluang cuan hyrox setelah tren padel?","https://theconversation.com/selamat-datang-era-fitness-entertainment-bagaimana-peluang-cuan-hyrox-setelah-tren-padel-277854"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Ketika simbol militer menjadi bagian dari gaya hidup"]},{"k":"p","s":["Bagi penggemar kebugaran, perlengkapan militer yang dipamerkan mungkin sekadar tantangan untuk menguji kekuatan, daya tahan, dan memberikan pengalaman unik baru. Namun, ada hal yang penting diamati dalam konteks ini."]},{"k":"p","s":[["Sosiolog Erving Goffman","https://ejurnal.ubk.ac.id/oratio/en/article/view/63?utm"]," menjelaskan bahwa interaksi sosial sebagai semacam pertunjukan. Dalam kehidupan sehari-hari, orang menampilkan identitas melalui penampilan, perilaku, bahasa, dan lingkungan. Semua itu membentuk kesan yang ditangkap orang lain."]},{"k":"p","s":["Kerangka ini membantu kita memahami bagaimana identitas militer ditampilkan dalam acara olahraga. Di arena yang dipenuhi pelari, penggemar fitness, keluarga, dan komunitas, prajurit tidak hanya tampil sebagai anggota institusi pertahanan, tetapi juga sebagai sesama peserta olahraga."]},{"k":"p","s":["Masalahnya, citra yang ditampilkan tidak pernah sepenuhnya netral. Ketika militer hadir melalui aktivitas yang menyenangkan, perhatian publik dapat lebih tertuju pada kebugaran, solidaritas, dan semangat kompetisi daripada pada kewenangan institusi tersebut atau batas perannya dalam negara demokratis."]},{"k":"p","s":["Di pihak lain, masyarakat sipil tidak sekadar menyaksikan simbol militer dari kejauhan, melainkan berinteraksi dengannya melalui pengalaman fisik."]},{"k":"p","s":[["Penelitian tentang olahraga dan militerisme Inggris","https://www.tandfonline.com/servlet/linkout?type=Scholix&url=https%3A%2F%2Fdx.doi.org%2F10.1177%252F0038038512453795"]," menunjukkan bagaimana budaya populer dan olahraga dapat membantu membangun citra kepahlawanan militer sekaligus menormalkan nilai-nilai militerisme."]},{"k":"p","s":["Temuan itu tidak otomatis membuktikan bahwa PRIMAROX memiliki agenda serupa, tetapi setidaknya memberi kerangka untuk mempertanyakan bagaimana simbol militer memperoleh penerimaan melalui ruang yang terasa jauh dari politik."]},{"k":"h","s":["Membaca arah relasi kuasa"]},{"k":"p","s":["Di arena olahraga, prajurit dan warga sipil tampak setara: sama-sama berlari, mengangkat beban, dan menghadapi tantangan fisik. Namun, kesetaraan sebagai peserta kompetisi tidak berarti kesetaraan dalam relasi kuasa."]},{"k":"p","s":["TNI memiliki kewenangan negara, struktur komando, dan fungsi pertahanan yang tidak dimiliki warga sipil. Karena itu, kehadiran militer di ruang publik tidak cukup dibaca sebagai pertemuan dua kelompok yang berbagi hobi. Kita juga perlu bertanya siapa yang memiliki kuasa menentukan batas keterlibatan militer dalam kehidupan sipil, serta bagaimana kewenangan itu diawasi."]},{"k":"p","s":["Pertanyaan tersebut relevan dalam konteks sejarah Indonesia. Pada masa Orde Baru, ",["doktrin Dwifungsi ABRI","https://ejournal.fisip.unjani.ac.id/index.php/jurnal-academia-praja/article/view/182"]," memberikan militer peran dalam pertahanan sekaligus kehidupan sosial-politik. Reformasi 1998 kemudian ",["mendorong perubahan hubungan sipil–militer","https://journal.unnes.ac.id/sju/jih/article/view/36973"],", termasuk pemisahan TNI dan Polri serta upaya memperkuat supremasi sipil."]},{"k":"p","s":["Kini, perdebatan kembali mengemuka setelah pengesahan ",["Undang-Undang Nomor 3 Tahun 2025","https://peraturan.bpk.go.id/Details/319166/uu-no-3-tahun-2025?utm"]," yang merevisi UU TNI."]},{"k":"p","s":["Perubahan ketentuan penempatan prajurit aktif di kementerian dan lembaga negara memunculkan kekhawatiran akademisi mengenai batas kewenangan militer dan pengawasan sipil. ",["Kajian Victor Imanuel W. Nalle pada 2026","https://repositori.ukdc.ac.id/id/eprint/2595/"]," juga menempatkan revisi tersebut dalam dinamika politik dan perubahan relasi sipil–militer pasca-Reformasi."]},{"k":"p","s":["Dalam konteks ini, persoalannya bukan membuktikan bahwa satu ajang olahraga menyebabkan militerisme, melainkan bagaimana keakraban simbolik dengan militer berkembang bersamaan dengan perdebatan mengenai perluasan peran institusinya."]},{"k":"h","s":["Dari keakraban menuju pertanyaan demokrasi"]},{"k":"p","s":["Olahraga bukan ruang yang terpisah dari politik–justru dapat menjadi tempat institusi membangun citra, memperoleh perhatian, dan membentuk hubungan dengan masyarakat."]},{"k":"p","s":["Ketika ",["simbol militer dikemas","https://journals.sagepub.com/doi/10.1177/0038038512453795"]," sebagai tantangan yang seru dan layak dibagikan di media sosial, citra institusi dapat ",["lebih mudah diterima","https://academic.oup.com/isr/article/23/3/1046/5866651"]," tanpa disertai pembicaraan mengenai akuntabilitas dan batas kewenangannya."]},{"k":"p","s":["Bagi generasi muda yang akrab dengan komunitas lari dan kebugaran, pertanyaan ini bukan ajakan untuk mencurigai setiap acara yang melibatkan TNI. Sebaliknya, ini merupakan ajakan untuk tidak berhenti pada pengalaman baru yang menyenangkan."]},{"k":"p","s":["Kita perlu membedakan penghargaan terhadap kemampuan individu prajurit dari penerimaan tanpa kritik terhadap institusi militer. Disiplin dan ketahanan fisik tidak dengan sendirinya membuktikan bahwa perluasan peran militer dalam urusan sipil dapat dibenarkan."]},{"k":"p","s":["Dalam demokrasi, kedekatan militer dengan masyarakat tidak boleh menggantikan kebutuhan akan pengawasan sipil. Sebab, yang perlu dijaga bukan sekadar batas antara arena olahraga dan arena politik, melainkan batas kewenangan antara institusi bersenjata dan masyarakat sipil."]},{"k":"p","s":["Keakraban militer dengan warga sipil seharusnya membuat kita semakin memahami peran militer dalam demokrasi–jangan sampai justru membuat kita semakin jarang mempertanyakannya."]}],"chars":6349},"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/kenya":{"r":"govuk","at":"2026-11-17T16:47Z","sha":"e5e4d098bc1cc9cadebfcc39585af322c2225087afe3ade228e5e5dbb2e68f0f","read":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/foreign-travel-advice/kenya","bytes":98206,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Kenya travel advice","by":[{"n":"Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","r":""}],"pub":"2013-03-19T00:00:00+00:00","mod":"2026-11-06T17:00:48+00:00","blocks":[{"k":"h","s":["Warnings and insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["Your travel insurance could be invalidated if you travel against advice from the Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO)."]},{"k":"h","s":["Areas where FCDO advises against travel"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Kenya-Somalia border and northern parts of the east coast"]},{"k":"p","s":["Due to the risk of terrorism from groups based in Somalia, FCDO advises against all travel to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["Mandera County"]},{"k":"li","s":["Tarbaj and Wajir East constituencies in Wajir County, except for Wajir Town"]},{"k":"li","s":["areas of Wajir County within 60km of Kenya’s border with Somalia"]},{"k":"li","s":["Garissa County - except for Garissa Town, the constituency of Lagdera and the areas of Balambala constituency which lie north and west of the main road which runs from Saka on the Tana River up to the intersection with the C81 Road"]},{"k":"li","s":["Lamu County, except for Lamu Island and Manda Island"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all but essential travel to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["Garissa Town"]},{"k":"li","s":["Tana River County north of the Tana River as far as the town of Saka"]},{"k":"li","s":["within 15km of the east coast between the Tana River and the Galana (Athi-Galana-Sabaki) River"]},{"k":"li","s":["Moyale Town and up to 5km around it, including to the border with Ethiopia"]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["why FCDO advises against travel","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/kenya/regional-risks"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Before you travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["No travel can be guaranteed safe. Read all the advice in this guide. You may also find it helpful to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for women travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/advice-for-women-travelling-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read our ",["guide on disability and travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/disabled-travellers"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read about ",["safety for solo and independent travel","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/solo-and-independent-travel"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["advice on volunteering and adventure travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/safer-adventure-travel-and-volunteering-overseas"]]},{"k":"hs","s":["Travel insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you choose to travel, research your destinations and ",["get appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"],". Insurance should cover your itinerary, planned activities and expenses in an emergency."]},{"k":"h","s":["About FCDO travel advice"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO provides advice about risks of travel to help you make informed decisions. Find out ",["more about FCDO travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/kenya/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Travel Aware on Instagram","https://www.instagram.com/travelaware/"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Entry requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["This information is for people travelling on a full ",["‘British citizen’ passport","https://www.gov.uk/types-of-british-nationality"]," from the UK. It is based on the UK government’s understanding of the current rules for the most common types of travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["The authorities in Kenya set and enforce entry rules. If you’re not sure how these requirements apply to you, contact the ",["Kenyan High Commission in the UK","https://www.kenyahighcom.org.uk/"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Passport validity requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["To enter Kenya, your passport must have an ‘expiry date’ at least 6 months after the date you arrive and at least 2 blank pages."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check with your travel provider that your passport and other travel documents meet requirements. ",["Renew your passport","https://www.gov.uk/renew-adult-passport/renew"]," if you need to."]},{"k":"p","s":["You will be denied entry if you do not have a valid travel document or try to use a passport that has been reported lost or stolen."]},{"k":"h","s":["Dual nationals"]},{"k":"p","s":["When returning to the UK, British citizens must carry a valid ",["British passport","https://www.gov.uk/browse/abroad/passports"]," or ",["certificate of entitlement","https://www.gov.uk/right-of-abode/apply-for-a-certificate-of-entitlement"],". See ",["Dual citizenship","https://www.gov.uk/dual-citizenship"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Visa requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["You must ",["apply online for electronic travel authorisation","https://www.etakenya.go.ke/en"]," in advance of travel. The local authorities recommend applying at least 2 weeks before your departure."]},{"k":"p","s":["Travellers who currently hold a visa can continue to travel using their visa until it expires."]},{"k":"p","s":["For information on work permits and residency, check the ",["Kenyan Department of Immigration","https://immigration.go.ke/"]," requirements."]},{"k":"h","s":["Mandatory travel insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["From 5 October 2026, most travellers visiting Kenya for less than 12 months must have Kenyan Government-provided travel health insurance."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you require an Electronic Travel Authorisation (eTA), you must buy this insurance as part of the application process. If you already hold a valid eTA, you must obtain the insurance through the ",["Kenyan eCitizen insurance portal","https://insurance.ecitizen.go.ke/dashboard"],". Foreign travel insurance policies are not accepted in place of this requirement."]},{"k":"p","s":["The insurance is valid for 90 days and can be used for multiple entries into Kenya during that period."]},{"k":"p","s":["The requirement does not apply to Kenyan citizens, holders of valid Kenyan residence status, citizens of East African Community partner states, or transit passengers that are not passing through Kenyan immigration control."]},{"k":"p","s":["You should also make sure you have travel insurance that covers your individual needs."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["To enter Kenya, you must have a certificate to prove you’ve had a yellow fever vaccination if you’re coming from a ",["country listed as a transmission risk","https://nathnacyfzone.org.uk/factsheet/65/countries-with-risk-of-yellow-fever-transmission"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["For full details about medical entry requirements and recommended vaccinations, see ",["TravelHealthPro’s Kenya guide","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/117/kenya#Vaccine_Recommendations"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Ebola screening"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Government of Kenya has confirmed cases of Ebola. Public health measures are in place, including contact tracing, surveillance, border screening and quarantine for people considered at risk."]},{"k":"p","s":["Travellers arriving in Kenya, particularly those coming from Uganda, Ethiopia and the Democratic Republic of Congo (DRC), may be subject to enhanced health screening measures due to the ongoing Ebola outbreak centred in the DRC. The World Health Organisation (WHO) has ",["declared this a Public Health Emergency of International Concern","https://www.who.int/news/item/17-05-2026-epidemic-of-ebola-disease-in-the-democratic-republic-of-the-congo-and-uganda-determined-a-public-health-emergency-of-international-concern"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["The Kenyan authorities provide public health information through the Jali Health Chatbot. To access the service, save +(254) 700 719 719 to your phone and send “Hello” by Whatsapp to access automated health information and guidance. This is not a staffed helpline."]},{"k":"h","s":["Customs rules"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are strict rules about ",["goods you can take into or out of Kenya","https://www.kenyagovisas.com/news/kenya-customs-regulations"],". You must declare anything that may be prohibited or subject to tax or duty."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Taking drones into Kenya"]},{"k":"p","s":["It is illegal to import or export drones without prior approval from the ",["Kenya Civil Aviation Authority (KCAA)","https://www.kcaa.or.ke/"],". Contact the KCAA well in advance of travel if you wish to bring a drone to Kenya."]},{"k":"h","s":["Safety and security"]},{"k":"p","s":["This guide also has safety advice for ",["regions of Kenya","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/kenya/regional-risks"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Terrorism"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high threat of terrorist attack globally affecting UK interests and British nationals, including from groups and individuals who view the UK and British nationals as targets. Stay aware of your surroundings at all times."]},{"k":"p","s":["UK Counter Terrorism Policing has information and advice on ",["staying safe","https://www.counterterrorism.police.uk/runhidetell/"]," and what to do in the event of a terrorist attack. Find out ",["how to reduce your risk from terrorism while abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/reduce-your-risk-from-terrorism-while-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Terrorism in Kenya"]},{"k":"p","s":["Terrorists are very likely to try to carry out attacks in Kenya."]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a heightened threat of terrorism across Kenya. Attacks could target westerners, including British nationals. These could occur at any time including at religious events, public holidays or celebrations. Attacks are indiscriminate and could occur in places visited by foreigners, including tourists, such as, but not limited to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["hotels, bars, restaurants and nightclubs"]},{"k":"li","s":["sporting events"]},{"k":"li","s":["supermarkets and shopping centres"]},{"k":"li","s":["beaches"]},{"k":"li","s":["safari parks"]},{"k":"li","s":["commercial and government buildings"]},{"k":"li","s":["places of worship"]},{"k":"li","s":["diplomatic premises"]},{"k":"p","s":["Be particularly alert in these places. If you go regularly to any location, try to vary timings and patterns of movement. Always travel during daylight hours if possible. Look at the security arrangements in buildings you visit, including bag searches, physical security and guards. The main terrorist threat is from extremists linked to Al Shabaab – an Al Qaida-affiliated militant group in Somalia. Al Shabaab has issued threats and carried out attacks against Kenya, in part, due to Kenyan military intervention in Somalia. See ",["Regional risks","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/kenya/regional-risks"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Recent significant attacks include :"]},{"k":"li","s":["in 2020 Al Shabaab conducted an attack on a military airstrip in Lamu County, killing 3 people"]},{"k":"li","s":["in 2019 there was an attack at the hotel and commercial complex at 14 Riverside in Nairobi, resulting in injuries and loss of life"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is some evidence of growing support for Daesh (formerly ISIL) in Kenya. On 4 January 2024 Daesh published a statement calling for a new global campaign of terrorism including a specific focus on western and Jewish targets. This statement and the ongoing conflict in Israel and Palestine could increase the likelihood of terrorist attacks that affect British nationals."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Lamu Island and Manda Island"]},{"k":"p","s":["Travellers to Lamu Island and Manda Island should be particularly vigilant given the close proximity of these islands to the Lamu County mainland. You should only travel to the islands by air to Lamu airport (a civilian airport on Manda Island), and not by road. The only commercial option for air travel to or from Lamu Island and Manda Island is through Lamu airport. See ",["Regional risks","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/kenya/regional-risks"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Terrorist kidnap"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high threat of terrorist kidnap across Kenya. You should be alert to the heightened threat of terrorist kidnapping targeting westerners, including British nationals. Westerners have been the target of kidnaps in northern counties bordering Somalia and coastal counties. Further kidnaps are very likely."]},{"k":"p","s":["British nationals are seen as legitimate targets, including tourists, humanitarian aid workers, journalists and business travellers. If you are kidnapped, the reason for your presence is unlikely to protect you or secure your safe release."]},{"k":"p","s":["The long-standing policy of the British government is not to make substantive concessions to hostage takers. The British government considers that paying ransoms and releasing prisoners builds the capability of terrorist groups and finances their activities. This can, in turn, increase the risk of further hostage-taking. The Terrorism Act (2000) makes payments to terrorists illegal."]},{"k":"h","s":["Political situation"]},{"k":"p","s":["Protests, demonstrations and strikes are common in Kenya, particularly in Nairobi. These events often cause traffic disruption and can lead to violence. A number of demonstrators have been injured and killed in recent years. The situation could change quickly, especially on key dates, such as anniversaries of previous protests. Stay away from political gatherings and large crowds and monitor local media to see when and where major protests are likely. Follow local news and the instructions of local authorities closely."]},{"k":"h","s":["Crime"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are frequent incidents of violent crime including mugging, armed robbery and carjacking, particularly in the large cities and on major highways."]},{"k":"p","s":["Although uncommon, violent crimes have resulted in the deaths of British nationals, including during daylight hours."]},{"k":"p","s":["Avoid walking alone in isolated areas, including in daylight. Criminals might target you directly, so be aware of your surroundings and make sure people know where you are and when you are due to return. The risks are higher in some areas of major cities."]},{"k":"p","s":["In Nairobi:"]},{"k":"li","s":["Eastleigh"]},{"k":"li","s":["Central Business District"]},{"k":"li","s":["Mathare, Kibera and slum areas"]},{"k":"p","s":["In Mombasa:"]},{"k":"li","s":["in the Old Town"]},{"k":"li","s":["on and around the Likoni Ferry, which links Mombasa to the southern resorts"]},{"k":"p","s":["Crime rates are often higher around the Christmas and New Year period so take extra precautions at this time of year."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Protecting your belongings"]},{"k":"p","s":["Bag-snatching is common in bus stations, railway stations and airports. Be vigilant and take note of any security advice given by your hotel, employer or your hosts. If you’re attacked, do not resist. Avoid carrying large sums of money or wearing expensive-looking jewellery or watches."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Vehicle crime"]},{"k":"p","s":["Always drive with windows closed and doors locked. When driving outside of cities and in remote areas, consider driving in convoy. Avoid driving at night if possible. Carjackers may set up bogus checkpoints. See ",["Transport risks","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/kenya/safety-and-security#transport-risks"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Scams"]},{"k":"p","s":["Beware of thieves posing as police officers or private security guards. It’s a technique used by criminals to take charge of valuables, passports and vehicles and steal them. Always ask for identification."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Drink and food spiking"]},{"k":"p","s":["Do not accept drinks or food from strangers in bars or clubs. Criminals spike drinks to weaken and confuse their victims and then commit theft or sexual assault."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Methanol poisoning"]},{"k":"p","s":["There has been an increase in cases of serious illness caused by alcoholic drinks containing methanol in popular travel destinations around the world."]},{"k":"p","s":["Even small amounts of methanol can kill. It is not possible to identify methanol in alcoholic drinks by taste or smell. See ",["Travel Aware Spiking and methanol poisoning","https://travelaware.campaign.gov.uk/spiking-and-methanol-poisoning/"]," for information about how to reduce the risks."]},{"k":"p","s":["Seek urgent medical attention if you or someone you are travelling with show the ",["signs of methanol poisoning","https://travelaware.campaign.gov.uk/spiking-and-methanol-poisoning/"]," after drinking."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Attacks and sexual assault"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sexual assaults are rare, but do happen, and can affect both male and female travellers."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Social media and dating apps"]},{"k":"p","s":["Criminals can use dating apps to identify victims to rob or sexually assault. There has been an increase in criminals targeting LGBT+ travellers in particular. Be cautious when using social media and dating apps. If you decide to meet someone, meet in a well-lit, public place and make sure that someone knows where you are."]},{"k":"h","s":["Laws and cultural differences"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Personal ID"]},{"k":"p","s":["You must always carry ID. A copy of your passport is normally acceptable, but police officers may insist on seeing the original document so keep it within a reasonable travelling distance."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Dress code"]},{"k":"p","s":["The coastal areas of Kenya are mainly Muslim. Show courtesy by dressing conservatively away from tourist resorts and hotels – particularly in Mombasa. Wearing holiday-style clothing is likely to get negative attention at religious sites or buildings."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Smoking and e-cigarette bans"]},{"k":"p","s":["It is illegal to smoke in any public place in Kenya, except in designated smoking areas. If you smoke in a prohibited place, you could get a fine of up to 50,000 Kenyan shillings or up to 6 months in prison."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Illegal drugs and prison sentences"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re convicted of using illegal drugs in Kenya, you will get a heavy fine and prison sentence. The penalty for possession is up to 10 years in prison. People found to be trafficking illegal drugs could face life imprisonment."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Using cameras in secure areas"]},{"k":"p","s":["It is illegal to take photographs of official buildings, including embassies, or at airports. You could be arrested if caught."]},{"k":"hs","s":["LGBT+ travellers"]},{"k":"p","s":["Same-sex sexual activity is illegal and same-sex relationships are not tolerated in Kenya’s conservative society. Showing affection in public could lead to arrest and imprisonment. See the ‘Social media and dating apps’ subheading for more advice."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more ",["advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Wildlife, animal products and souvenirs"]},{"k":"p","s":["It is illegal to buy, sell, kill or capture any protected wild animal or trade any of its parts without a licence. If you are caught buying or trafficking banned goods, you could face a fine or prison sentence."]},{"k":"h","s":["Outdoor activities and adventure tourism"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Game reserves and national parks"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re visiting game reserves, use reputable tour operators and arrive at your destination in daylight hours. Do not buy safari tours from touts. Always follow park regulations and advice from wardens."]},{"k":"p","s":["There are risks associated with viewing wildlife, particularly on foot or at close range. Swimming in rivers and lakes is illegal in national parks and is best avoided elsewhere due the dangers from wildlife and waterborne diseases."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Hiking and mountaineering"]},{"k":"p","s":["You must hire a local guide on certain hikes in Kenya. Be conscious of the risk from wildlife and do not approach wild animals. Make sure your travel insurance covers all your planned activities."]},{"k":"p","s":["Altitude sickness is a risk when hiking in high-altitude areas, including on Mount Kenya. Read about ",["altitude sickness on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/26/altitude-illness"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Transport risks"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are planning to drive in Kenya, see ",["information on driving abroad","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["You can use a UK photocard driving licence in Kenya for up to 3 months. If you still have a paper driving licence, you may need to ",["update it to a photocard licence","https://www.gov.uk/exchange-paper-driving-licence"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["After 3 months, you’ll need to have both the ",["1968 version of the international driving permit (IDP)","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad/international-driving-permit"]," and your UK driving licence with you in the car. You cannot buy an IDP outside the UK, so get one before you travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re staying longer or living in Kenya, you’ll need to get a Kenyan driving licence."]},{"k":"p","s":["Driving standards are often poor. There is a risk of vehicle crime – see ",["Crime","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/kenya/safety-and-security#crime"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Jomo Kenyatta International Airport to Nairobi City"]},{"k":"p","s":["For travel between Jomo Kenyatta International Airport and Nairobi City, use the Mombasa Road or the Nairobi Expressway. There is a higher risk of carjacking on the old airport road (Airport South Road) and Jogoo Road."]},{"k":"p","s":["The Mombasa Road can get very busy during rush hour, and check-in can take several hours. Allow plenty of time to get to the airport. A vehicle security check outside the airport may add to your journey time."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Travel in remote areas"]},{"k":"p","s":["Monitor local media and take care in all remote areas. ",["The Kenya Tourism Federation Safety and Communication Center","https://ktf.co.ke/?page_id=857"]," provides tourist advice and emergency help."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Bus travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["There have been serious accidents involving long-distance buses and minibuses (‘matatus’). The accidents are often due to poor maintenance and speeding. Often minibuses are uninsured. Check operators’ safety standards."]},{"k":"p","s":["There are frequent minibus hijackings and robberies."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Driving fines"]},{"k":"p","s":["On-the-spot fines from traffic police are common but illegal. If a traffic police officer stops you, ask them to issue you with the correct paperwork."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Air travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you charter a private aircraft, check with the company about the condition of the aircraft and runways. If the air crew does not include a safety pilot, qualified to take over the controls, find another company that does."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Rail travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["Passenger trains run between Nairobi and Mombasa. Take care of your belongings while on the train and at railway stations. If you leave your compartment, take your valuables with you."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Sea travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["Piracy and armed robbery off the coast of Somalia, in the Gulf of Aden and Indian Ocean remain a significant threat."]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["piracy and armed robbery at sea","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/sea-river-and-piracy-safety"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Extreme weather and natural disasters"]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out what you can do to ",["prepare for and respond to extreme weather and natural hazards","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/tropical-cyclones"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Earthquakes"]},{"k":"p","s":["Kenya lies on an active fault and tremors occur from time to time. The last significant earthquake to affect the region was of magnitude 5.2 in 2007."]},{"k":"p","s":["The US Federal Emergency Management Agency has advice about what to do before, during and after an earthquake."]},{"k":"h","s":["Regional risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["This section has safety advice for regions of Kenya. It only covers regions where FCDO has specific advice."]},{"k":"p","s":["You should also read ",["FCDO’s overall travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/kenya"]," and ",["safety and security advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/kenya/safety-and-security"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Kenya-Somalia border and northern parts of the east coast"]},{"k":"p","s":["Due to the risk of terrorism from groups based in Somalia, FCDO advises against all travel to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["Mandera County"]},{"k":"li","s":["Tarbaj and Wajir East constituencies in Wajir County, except for Wajir Town"]},{"k":"li","s":["areas of Wajir County within 60km of Kenya’s border with Somalia"]},{"k":"li","s":["Garissa County - except for Garissa Town, the constituency of Lagdera and the areas of Balambala constituency which lie north and west of the main road which runs from Saka on the Tana River up to the intersection with the C81 Road"]},{"k":"li","s":["Lamu County, except for Lamu Island and Manda Island"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all but essential travel to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["Garissa Town"]},{"k":"li","s":["Tana River County north of the Tana River as far as the town of Saka"]},{"k":"li","s":["within 15km of the east coast between the Tana River and the Galana (Athi-Galana-Sabaki) River"]},{"k":"li","s":["Moyale Town and up to 5km around it, including to the border with Ethiopia"]},{"k":"p","s":["There have been frequent attacks in the north-eastern border regions, most of which were attributed to Al Shabaab."]},{"k":"p","s":["Attacks have killed members of the Kenyan security forces as well as civilians. The Kenyan security forces have increased their presence in the affected areas. Armed militia groups operate within the Boni National Reserve and along the border with Somalia. See ",["Terrorism","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/kenya/safety-and-security#terrorism"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Lamu Island and Manda Island"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you travel to Lamu Island or Manda Island, you should fly to Lamu Airport (a civilian airport on Manda Island). Do not travel by road. See ",["Terrorism","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/kenya/safety-and-security#terrorism"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Jomo Kenyatta International Airport to Nairobi City"]},{"k":"p","s":["For travel between Jomo Kenyatta International Airport and Nairobi City, you should use the Mombasa Road or the Nairobi Expressway. See ",["Transport risks","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/kenya/safety-and-security#transport-risks"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["North and north-east Kenya"]},{"k":"p","s":["Rural areas, particularly in the north and north-east of Kenya, occasionally experience cattle rustling, banditry and ethnic clashes. Foreign nationals are not usually the target, but you should take great care."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Turkana, West Pokot, Elgeyo-Marakwet, Baringo,Samburu, Laikipia, Meru and Isiolo counties"]},{"k":"p","s":["Security operations continue in parts of these counties due to banditry ,cattle rustling and intercommunal violence. While previous dusk-to-dawn curfews have largely been lifted, movement restrictions may still be introduced during security operations, particularly in hotspots such as the Turkana–West Pokot border, Kerio Valley (Elgeyo-Marakwet) and remote areas of Samburu, and Baringo. Follow local security measures and use caution."]},{"k":"h","s":["Kenya-Ethiopia border"]},{"k":"p","s":["Since October 2026, violence in the Ethiopian town of Moyale has affected the border area, including on the Kenyan side. There have been reports of stray gunfire, unexploded ordnance and projectiles landing in and up to 3km around the Kenyan town of Moyale, resulting in fatalities and injuries. There have also been reports of disruption at the Moyale border crossing. The security situation remains unpredictable and could deteriorate without warning."]},{"k":"p","s":["If crossing the Kenya-Ethiopia border at Moyale, stay alert to developments and follow the instructions of local authorities. Vehicles crossing the Kenya-Ethiopia border at Moyale should stay on the A2 road and travel directly to Marsabit before breaking your journey."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check ",["FCDO Travel Advice for Ethiopia","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/ethiopia"]," before crossing the border."]},{"k":"h","s":["Mount Elgon"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a significant security presence in Mount Elgon because of armed clashes. Further incidents are possible. Seek local advice before you set off."]},{"k":"h","s":["Health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Before you travel check that:"]},{"k":"li","s":["your destination can provide the healthcare you may need"]},{"k":"li","s":["you have ",["appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"]," for local treatment or unexpected medical evacuation"]},{"k":"p","s":["This is particularly important if you have a health condition or are pregnant."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency medical number"]},{"k":"p","s":["Dial 999 and ask for an ambulance."]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your insurance company quickly if you’re referred to a medical facility for treatment."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine recommendations and health risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["At least 8 weeks before your trip:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check the latest ",["vaccine recommendations for Kenya","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/117/kenya#Vaccine_Recommendations"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see where to get vaccines and whether you have to pay on the ",["NHS travel vaccinations page","https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/travel-vaccinations/"]]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["what health risks you’ll face in Kenya","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/117/kenya"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["malaria and dengue"]},{"k":"li","s":["Zika virus"]},{"k":"li","s":["schistosomiasis"]},{"k":"li","s":["mpox"]},{"k":"li","s":["ebola"]},{"k":"p","s":["Altitude sickness is a risk in parts of Kenya. Read more about ",["altitude sickness on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/26/altitude-illness"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Ebola"]},{"k":"p","s":["On 6 October 2026, the Kenyan Ministry of Health confirmed its first imported case of Ebola. The government is continuing to implement public health measures in response, including contact tracing, surveillance, and border screening, as well as quarantine arrangements for individuals deemed at risk. Follow the advice of local authorities and monitor updates from the ",["Kenyan Ministry of Health","https://www.health.go.ke/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["TravelHealthPro has information on ",["Ebola Disease","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/news/ebola-disease-in-drc-and-uganda"]," and ",["general information on Ebola and similar diseases","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheets/viral-haemorrhagic-fever"],". Some countries may have additional health screening requirements for travellers arriving from Kenya. ",["Check entry requirements","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice"]," for countries you are travelling to or transiting through."]},{"k":"p","s":["UK Health Security Agency has ",["Ebola information for humanitarian or healthcare workers","https://www.gov.uk/government/collections/ebola-virus-disease-clinical-management-and-guidance"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Medication"]},{"k":"p","s":["The legal status and regulation of some medicines prescribed or bought in the UK can be different in other countries."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["best practice when travelling with medicines on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/43/medicines-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Healthcare in Kenya"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has a list of ",["medical facilities in Kenya","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/kenya-list-of-medical-facilities/kenya-doctors"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["There is also ",["guidance on healthcare if you’re living in Kenya","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/living-in-kenya"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travel and mental health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["FCDO guidance on travel and mental health","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-advice-for-people-with-mental-health-issues"],". There is also ",["mental health guidance on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/85/travelling-with-mental-health-conditions"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Getting help"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) cannot provide tailored advice for individual trips. Read this travel advice and carry out your own research before deciding whether to travel."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency services in Kenya"]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 999 (ambulance, fire, police)"]},{"k":"h","s":["Kenya Tourism Federation"]},{"k":"p","s":["Kenya Tourism Federation’s ",["Safety and Communication Center","https://ktf.co.ke/?page_id=857"]," provides tourist advice and emergency help."]},{"k":"h","s":["Contact your travel provider and insurer"]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your travel provider and your insurer if you are involved in a serious incident or emergency abroad. They will tell you if they can help and what you need to do."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Refunds and changes to travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["For refunds or changes to travel, contact your travel provider. You may also be able to make a claim through insurance. However, insurers usually require you to talk to your travel provider first."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["changing or cancelling travel plans","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice#changing-or-cancelling-travel-plans"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["where to get advice if you are in a dispute with a provider"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to access previous versions of travel advice to support a claim"]},{"k":"h","s":["Support from FCDO"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has guidance on staying safe and what to do if you need help or support abroad, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["finding ",["lawyers","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/lawyers?country=Kenya"]," and ",["funeral directors","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/funeral-directors?country=Kenya"]," in Kenya"]},{"k":"li","s":["dealing with a ",["death in Kenya","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/kenya-bereavement-information"]]},{"k":"li","s":["being ",["arrested or imprisoned in Kenya","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/kenya-prisoner-pack"]]},{"k":"li","s":["getting help if you’re a ",["victim of crime","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/victim-of-crime-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["getting help if you’ve been a ",["victim of rape or sexual assault in Kenya","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/kenya-information-for-victims-of-rape-and-sexual-assault/kenya-information-for-victims-of-rape-and-sexual-assault"]]},{"k":"li","s":["what to do if you’re ",["in hospital","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/in-hospital-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["if you’re ",["affected by a crisis","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"],", such as a terrorist attack"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contacting FCDO"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help abroad"]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["how to get help from the UK government abroad","https://www.contact.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/posts/kenya/british-high-commission-nairobi"]," including in an emergency."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help in the UK"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can call FCDO in London if you need urgent help because something has happened to a friend or relative abroad."]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 020 7008 5000 (24 hours)"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Find out about call charges","https://www.gov.uk/call-charges"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/kenya/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Risk information for British companies"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Overseas Business Risk service offers ",["information and advice for British companies operating in Keny","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/overseas-business-risk-kenya"]," a on how to manage political, economic, and business security-related risks."]}],"chars":25625,"change":"FCDO now advises against all but essential travel to Moyale Town and up to 5km around it, including to the border with Ethiopia. Updated information about the Kenya-Ethiopia border ('Warnings and insurance' and 'Regional risks' pages)."},"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/tajikistan":{"r":"govuk","at":"2026-11-17T17:18Z","sha":"6b2f32a22430ce86ffb30d773fe473c5996d39d21149ad237034ca79d3d093f9","read":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/foreign-travel-advice/tajikistan","bytes":69831,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Tajikistan travel advice","by":[{"n":"Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","r":""}],"pub":"2013-02-07T00:00:00+00:00","mod":"2026-08-19T15:15:52+01:00","blocks":[{"k":"h","s":["Warnings and insurance"]},{"k":"h","s":["Global travel impacts due to escalation in the Middle East"]},{"k":"p","s":["Escalation in the Middle East has caused widespread travel disruption, including airspace closures, delayed and cancelled flights."]},{"k":"p","s":["Your travel plans may be affected, even if your destination is not in the Middle East. Before you travel:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check travel advice for any countries or territories you are transiting through"]},{"k":"li","s":["check for the latest updates from your airline or tour operator"]},{"k":"li","s":["review your travel insurance policy for coverage"]},{"k":"li","s":["monitor local and international media for the latest information and sign up for travel advice email alerts."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you have been impacted by travel disruption and need to review your Tajik visa, contact the Tajik ",["Ministry of Foreign Affairs.","https://mfa.tj/en"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Before you travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["No travel can be guaranteed safe. Read all the advice in this guide. You may also find it helpful to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for women travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/advice-for-women-travelling-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read our ",["guide on disability and travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/disabled-travellers"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read about ",["safety for solo and independent travel","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/solo-and-independent-travel"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["advice on volunteering and adventure travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/safer-adventure-travel-and-volunteering-overseas"]]},{"k":"hs","s":["Travel insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you choose to travel, research your destinations and ",["get appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"],". Insurance should cover your itinerary, planned activities and expenses in an emergency."]},{"k":"h","s":["About FCDO travel advice"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) provides advice about risks of travel to help you make informed decisions. Find out ",["more about FCDO travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/tajikistan/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Travel Aware on Instagram","https://www.instagram.com/accounts/login/?next=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.instagram.com%2Ftravelaware%2F&is_from_rle"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Entry requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["This information is for people travelling on a full ",["‘British citizen’ passport","https://www.gov.uk/types-of-british-nationality"]," from the UK. It is based on the UK government’s understanding of Tajikistan’s current rules for the most common types of travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["The authorities in Tajikistan set and enforce entry rules. If you’re not sure how these requirements apply to you, contact the ",["Tajik Embassy in the UK","https://mfa.tj/en/london/contacts"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Passport validity requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["To enter Tajikistan, your passport must have an ‘expiry date’ at least 6 months after the date you arrive and have at least 2 blank pages."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check with your travel provider that your passport and other travel documents meet requirements. ",["Renew your passport","https://www.gov.uk/renew-adult-passport/renew"]," if you need to."]},{"k":"p","s":["You will be denied entry if you do not have a valid travel document or try to use a passport that has been reported lost or stolen."]},{"k":"h","s":["Dual nationals"]},{"k":"p","s":["When returning to the UK, British citizens must carry a valid ",["British passport","https://www.gov.uk/browse/abroad/passports"]," or ",["certificate of entitlement","https://www.gov.uk/right-of-abode/apply-for-a-certificate-of-entitlement"],". See ",["Dual citizenship","https://www.gov.uk/dual-citizenship"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Visa requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["You must have a visa to enter Tajikistan. If you arrive without a valid visa, you may be detained and refused entry. Travellers who have arrived without the correct documentation have been fined and deported. You will be required to pay for any ticket out of Tajikistan."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re entering Tajikistan on a visa, check it and carefully note the date of expiry and the number of entries permitted."]},{"k":"p","s":["Do not overstay your visa, or exceed your permitted duration of stay, even for a very short period. If you overstay your visa, you could get a fine and will not be allowed to leave Tajikistan until you get an exit visa. You can pay for an exit visa at the Ministry of Foreign Affairs Consular Office. Once you’re in Tajikistan, you can apply for a visa extension at the ",["Consular Department of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs","https://consular.tj/"],". Most visa categories can be extended in Tajikistan. However, Tourist Visas (T visas) cannot be extended. If you are travelling on a Tourist Visa, you must leave the country before your visa expires. For further information on visa requirements and extensions, visit ",["Consular Department of the MFA","https://consular.tj/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Exit visas are not available at airports in Tajikistan. If you’re travelling overland, make sure you arrive at your intended border crossing in good time before your period of stay or visa expires."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Applying for a visa"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Apply online for an e-visa","https://www.evisa.tj/index.evisa.html"]," from the Tajikistan Ministry of Foreign Affairs before travelling or for a physical visa on arrival (must be pre-approved). Carefully review the guidance provided on the Tajikistan e-visa website on length of visa validity. Your e-visa will only be valid for 60 days after approval. Make sure you get the correct type of visa and that it will be valid for the duration of your visit. British nationals have been turned away with incorrect visas. Allow at least two weeks for processing."]},{"k":"p","s":["You may be asked to provide proof of hotel bookings and any arrangements booked through a tour operator to be issued with a tourist visa or e-visa. This is usually requested in the form of a letter of invitation (LoI), a formal letter addressed to either the applicant or consular office by a Tajik-based sponsor providing details of the applicant and sponsor."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Travelling through Tajikistan"]},{"k":"p","s":["You must have a transit visa to travel through Tajikistan on your way to another country. These are usually valid for 3 days. If you need to stay longer, you must seek an extension from the ",["Ministry of Foreign Affairs","https://old.consular.tj/visa.aspx"]," once you arrive."]},{"k":"h","s":["Registering with the authorities"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are entering Tajikistan without an e-visa and staying for longer than 10 days, you must register with the Office for Registration of Foreign Citizens (OVIR) located at 5 Mirzo Tursunzoda Street, Dushanbe. Hotels are no longer permitted to complete the registration on your behalf. If you later stay at different addresses, you must register again separately."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you do not follow the registration procedure, you may not be allowed to leave Tajikistan until your registration process is resolved. This may result in fines or detention. There have been cases where lack of registration has resulted in detention at Dushanbe airport."]},{"k":"h","s":["Tajik-British dual nationality"]},{"k":"p","s":["Tajikistan does not recognise dual British nationality if the person concerned is also a Tajik national. If you enter Tajikistan with dual UK-Tajik nationality, the British Embassy will only be able to provide limited consular assistance. If you’re arrested or detained, the Tajik authorities are unlikely to allow you to get help from the British Embassy."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travel permit for the Gorno-Badakhshan Region"]},{"k":"p","s":["You must get a separate travel permit, in addition to a Tajik visa, to travel to the Gorno-Badakhshan Autonomous Region. If you’re in the UK, contact the ",["Tajik Embassy","https://mfa.tj/en/london"]," to apply for a permit before you travel. If you’re in Tajikistan, contact the ",["Consular Department of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs","https://old.consular.tj/Default_en.aspx"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["The Tajikistan government sometimes stops issuing permits to tourists at short notice due to security concerns. The Tajik Embassy can tell you whether the government is issuing permits for travel to the Gorno-Badakhshan Autonomous Region."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travel permit for the Khatlon Region"]},{"k":"p","s":["You must get a permit, in addition to a Tajik visa, to travel to areas within 20km of the border with Afghanistan in the Khatlon Region, including Panj and Kumsangir. Apply for a permit from the ",["Consular Department of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs","https://old.consular.tj/Default_en.aspx"]," in Dushanbe before you travel to the Khatlon region."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["For details about medical entry requirements and recommended vaccinations, see ",["TravelHealthPro’s Tajikistan guide","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/219/tajikistan#Vaccine_Recommendations"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["HIV screening"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you plan to stay for more than 90 days, you must show a medical certificate that you’re HIV-free or take a test. FCDO advises against taking the test in Tajikistan due to the poor quality of medical facilities."]},{"k":"h","s":["Customs rules"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are strict rules about goods you can take into or out of Tajikistan. You must declare anything that may be prohibited or subject to tax or duty. Foreign nationals travelling to Tajikistan should be aware of the country’s customs regulations regarding the import and export of cash:"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Bringing cash into Tajikistan"]},{"k":"p","s":["Travellers may bring up to $10,000 US dollars (or equivalent in other currencies) into Tajikistan without declaring it at customs. Any amount exceeding this should be declared before entry. Travellers may take up to $3,000 US dollars (or equivalent) out of the country without declaration. If the amount exceeds $10,000 US dollars, travellers must present documentation confirming the origin of the funds."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Customs declaration forms"]},{"k":"p","s":["Customs declaration forms are available in Russian and English. It is recommended to retain your entry declaration form until departure to prove the amount of money originally brought into the country. Failure to declare or provide documentation may result in fines or delays at the border."]},{"k":"h","s":["Safety and security"]},{"k":"p","s":["This guide also has safety advice for ",["regions of Tajikistan","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/tajikistan/regional-risks"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Terrorism"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high threat of terrorist attack globally affecting UK interests and British nationals, including from groups and individuals who view the UK and British nationals as targets. Stay aware of your surroundings at all times."]},{"k":"p","s":["UK Counter Terrorism Policing has information and advice on ",["staying safe","https://www.counterterrorism.police.uk/runhidetell/"]," and what to do in the event of a terrorist attack. Find out ",["how to reduce your risk from terrorism while abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/reduce-your-risk-from-terrorism-while-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Terrorism in Tajikistan"]},{"k":"p","s":["Terrorists are likely to try to carry out attacks in Tajikistan."]},{"k":"p","s":["Terrorist attacks could be indiscriminate, including in places frequented by foreign nationals, such as:"]},{"k":"li","s":["transport hubs"]},{"k":"li","s":["embassies"]},{"k":"li","s":["religious sites and places of worship"]},{"k":"li","s":["sporting and cultural events"]},{"k":"li","s":["shopping centres and crowded places"]},{"k":"p","s":["Examples of previous significant attacks include:"]},{"k":"li","s":["in March 2024, a plot to attack New Year (Nowruz) celebrations in Vahdat using poison was disrupted by Tajik authorities"]},{"k":"li","s":["in 2023, three suspected terrorists were reportedly killed by Tajik border forces while planning an attack ahead of Tajik national day celebrations. There are infrequent incursions by armed criminal and terrorist groups across the Afghanistan border into Tajikistan, mainly at night"]},{"k":"p","s":["Stay aware of your surroundings and take particular care during periods of national or religious significance and on public holidays, including Nowruz, Independence Day and New Year Celebrations. Keep up to date with local media reports and follow the advice of local authorities."]},{"k":"h","s":["Political situation"]},{"k":"p","s":["Avoid demonstrations or large gatherings of people, which are likely to attract a heavy presence from security forces. Use caution and maintain a high level of security awareness, particularly in public places. Be alert to any security announcements by the Tajik authorities."]},{"k":"h","s":["Crime"]},{"k":"p","s":["There have been occasional muggings and petty crime against foreigners in Dushanbe. Pickpocketing is common in crowded places such as markets and on public transport. Criminals may target foreigners as they are assumed to be carrying valuable items. Keep valuables in a safe place and out of public view."]},{"k":"p","s":["Use caution and take measures to reduce your personal risk, such as:"]},{"k":"li","s":["keep sight of your belongings at all times"]},{"k":"li","s":["be aware of thieves using distraction techniques"]},{"k":"li","s":["avoid carrying all your valuables together in one place e.g. handbags or pockets"]},{"k":"li","s":["consider avoiding walking alone at night"]},{"k":"li","s":["exercise a similar level of caution as you would in the UK"]},{"k":"li","s":["do not use unofficial taxis or a taxi already occupied by a passenger, particularly at night. Consider using private cars or pre-arranged taxis"]},{"k":"li","s":["do not show large amounts of money and be wary of strangers offering help or being over-friendly"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Bank card fraud"]},{"k":"p","s":["Fraudsters can steal your card details without you noticing. Use ATMs inside banks if possible, and check ATMs on the street for signs of tampering. Keep cards in sight when paying in shops and restaurants. Read ",["more about how to avoid bank card fraud","https://www.actionfraud.police.uk/a-z-of-fraud/bank-card-and-cheque-fraud"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Drink spiking and sexual assault"]},{"k":"p","s":["There have been cases of sexual assault, including rape, reported to the British Embassy. This includes suspected use of ‘date rape’ drugs targeting foreigners. Alcohol and drugs can lead to you being less alert, less in control and less aware of your environment. You should:"]},{"k":"li","s":["not leave drinks unattended"]},{"k":"li","s":["not accept drinks from strangers"]},{"k":"li","s":["be aware of how much you are drinking"]},{"k":"li","s":["not accept lifts from strangers or acquaintances at any time"]},{"k":"p","s":["Don’t split up from your friends, do not leave drinks unattended and do not go off with people you do not know. Save the location of your accommodation on your maps app, so it’s easy to find. See ",["TravelAware ‘Stick with your mates’","https://travelaware.campaign.gov.uk/#stick_with_your_mates"]," for tips and advice."]},{"k":"h","s":["Intimidation at Dushanbe International Airport"]},{"k":"p","s":["There have been cases of harassment by officials at Dushanbe International Airport. This includes requests for payment for allegedly incorrect documentation or other offences. Check with your hotel that your documentation and papers are in order before passing through border control at the airport. If you’re harassed or intimidated, report it to your travel agent or the consular bureau at the airport."]},{"k":"h","s":["Laws and cultural differences"]},{"k":"p","s":["Tajikistan has a secular constitution. Most Tajik citizens are Muslims and may be conservative, particularly in rural areas. Respect local traditions, customs, laws and religions at all times. Make sure your actions do not offend other cultures or religious beliefs, especially during the holy month of Ramadan or when you visit religious areas sites."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Ramadan"]},{"k":"p","s":["Ramadan is a holy month for Muslims. The dates vary by year and country. Cafés and restaurants may amend their menus and be busy around fast-breaking (‘Iftar’). Areas around mosques are also likely to be busy around prayer times. Be particularly aware of religious sensitivities at this time."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Personal ID"]},{"k":"p","s":["You must carry your passport, or a notarised copy of it, with you at all times. The police can arrest you if you do not carry ID. You can get a copy of your passport notarised in the UK and translated into Tajik or Russian, or use a copy notarised in Tajikistan."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Alcohol laws and bans"]},{"k":"p","s":["The legal age for purchasing alcohol is 18. If you appear to be drunk, the police can take you to a police station and issue you with a fine or detain you in a police cell overnight."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Smoking ban"]},{"k":"p","s":["It is illegal to smoke on the street in Tajikistan, and punishable by a fine."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Illegal drugs and prison sentences"]},{"k":"p","s":["Possession of drugs is illegal. You can get a lengthy prison sentence if convicted. Prison conditions are basic."]},{"k":"p","s":["The police may conduct drug raids in bars and night clubs. Stay calm and follow instructions."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Woman travelling alone"]},{"k":"p","s":["Women travelling alone in Tajikistan may receive unwanted attention, harassment or other difficulties. Consider not going out alone at night. See ",["advice for women travelling abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/advice-for-women-travelling-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Using cameras in secure areas"]},{"k":"p","s":["It is illegal to take photos of or use drones near anything related to the military or security, including border checkpoints, military sites and police stations. Check carefully that you are not near any military or security facilities. The Tajik authorities may ask you not to photograph government buildings."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Drones"]},{"k":"p","s":["The possession or use of drones or UAVs is prohibited unless you have permission from the Tajik National Security Committee. If you are found using drones without permission, you may be detained and your equipment confiscated."]},{"k":"hs","s":["LGBT+ travellers"]},{"k":"p","s":["Although same-sex sexual activity is not illegal under Tajik law, local attitudes are generally conservative and levels of tolerance and acceptance in society vary, particularly outside the main cities. Showing affection in public may receive unwanted and negative attention."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more ",["advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Money"]},{"k":"p","s":["Tajikistan is mainly a cash-only economy. Very few businesses accept credit cards and travellers’ cheques are not accepted. There is an increasing number of ATMs in Dushanbe and other larger towns, but none in rural areas. Most ATMs only accept Visa cards."]},{"k":"p","s":["Bring enough cash for your entire stay or withdraw cash from an ATM in Dushanbe ahead of any planned travel to other regions. Only change money at officially authorised currency exchanges."]},{"k":"p","s":["Tajik somoni is only available in Tajikistan. US dollars are the most easily exchanged and widely accepted foreign currency. Euros or Russian roubles are also easy to exchange. It may be difficult to exchange other currencies. Official exchange booths may not accept damaged or marked bank notes, nor will they accept US dollars issued before 2013."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Posting on social media"]},{"k":"p","s":["Be careful when posting images of your visit on social media. It is illegal to post images or comments on social media that show disrespect towards religion, culture or national symbols. If you share or publish images that the authorities consider to be insulting, you could get a fine or a prison sentence. Disrespectful content, including criticism of the government, could result in fines or detention."]},{"k":"h","s":["Outdoor activities and adventure tourism"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Trekking and mountaineering"]},{"k":"p","s":["Trekking in Tajikistan often involves travelling to very remote areas. There is a high risk of avalanches, landslides and rockfalls. Weather can change very quickly, and heavy rains or snowfall can block roads and trekking routes, particularly in the autumn and winter."]},{"k":"p","s":["At higher altitudes there is a possibility of snow in the summer months. Sunstroke and serious sunburn can also cause problems, particularly in mountainous areas."]},{"k":"p","s":["You should:"]},{"k":"li","s":["get appropriate insurance, including for any activity at high altitude"]},{"k":"li","s":["use a reputable trekking agency"]},{"k":"li","s":["let someone know where you are going and when you plan to return"]},{"k":"li","s":["not trek alone"]},{"k":"li","s":["adapt your plans to reflect local conditions and advice"]},{"k":"p","s":["In remote areas, mobile phone coverage is extremely limited, and medical facilities are basic. Most Tajik mobile phones have difficulties connecting to satellite phones. The difficult terrain can make access impossible in some cases."]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a limited mountain rescue service staffed by volunteers and rescue equipment they have is limited. This will be further limited in cases where individuals need rescuing at high altitudes or where weather conditions do not allow."]},{"k":"p","s":["Weather conditions can change rapidly at short notice, particularly in mountainous and high-altitude locations. The Ministry of Internal Affairs has a Tourist Police Section and the department can take calls 24/7 Tel (+99237) 231 80 36, Mobile phone (+992) 770 55 55 55."]},{"k":"h","s":["Transport risks"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are planning to drive in Tajikistan, see information on ",["driving abroad","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Driving licence and permit requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["You are permitted to drive in Tajikistan with a valid UK driving licence for up to 30 days. In addition, you must carry the 1968 version of the International Driving Permit (IDP) alongside your UK licence:"]},{"k":"li","s":["the IDP must be obtained before traveling, as it cannot be purchased outside the UK"]},{"k":"li","s":["while not legally required, it is strongly recommended to have your driving licence and IDP translated into Russian or Tajik to facilitate smoother interactions with local traffic authorities"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Driving your own vehicle"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can bring your personal vehicle into Tajikistan without paying import duties or taxes for a period of up to 60 days. After this period, you will need to pay a fee. You must declare your vehicle at the point of entry, carry both your vehicle registration documents and valid insurance that covers driving in Tajikistan."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Car rental considerations"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you plan to rent a vehicle in Tajikistan, be aware that rental companies may impose stricter requirements, such as:"]},{"k":"li","s":["a minimum age for drivers"]},{"k":"li","s":["at least one year of driving experience"]},{"k":"li","s":["mandatory possession of an IDP"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road rules and safety"]},{"k":"p","s":["Tajikistan enforces the following road laws:"]},{"k":"li","s":["drive on the right-hand side of the road"]},{"k":"li","s":["seatbelts must be worn by both drivers and all passengers"]},{"k":"li","s":["mobile phone use while driving is prohibited"]},{"k":"li","s":["there is a zero-tolerance policy for alcohol consumption while driving"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Driving conditions"]},{"k":"p","s":["Road infrastructure in Tajikistan can be challenging. Surfaces may be uneven or poorly maintained, especially in rural and mountainous areas, where areas may only be accessible by 4-wheel drive vehicles. Street lighting is often poor. Driving standards may vary significantly and can be unpredictable. Vehicles in Tajikistan are often poorly maintained. Petrol stations are rare outside towns and there are no breakdown companies. Make sure you take all you need for your journey and allow for delays. Consider bringing a satellite phone for travel outside towns to use in an emergency. Neighbouring countries may close borders temporarily."]},{"k":"p","s":["Conditions are particularly dangerous in spring due to the risk of avalanches and landslides."]},{"k":"p","s":["Many interior roads are only open in the summer months. It is possible to drive from Dushanbe to the north and Tajikistan’s second city, Khujand, using a tunnel. This road is particularly dangerous in winter due to icy conditions. Drivers can be trapped for a long time if caught in an avalanche due to the remote location."]},{"k":"p","s":["Flooding in the spring and winter often damages and closes roads in areas of the Gorno-Badakhshan Autonomous Region and other parts of the country. Many roads, including the Pamir Highway, are open but not fully repaired."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Taxis and buses"]},{"k":"p","s":["Use licensed taxis whenever possible. Unlicensed taxis can occasionally be found, despite licensing laws. Many taxis do not have rear seatbelts, so you may want to request a taxi that has them."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Air travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["In May 2022, the UK sanctioned Aeroflot, Rossiya Airlines and Ural Airlines. It is now illegal under UK law for any British national or British company to do business with these airlines. This includes buying flight tickets."]},{"k":"h","s":["Extreme weather and natural disasters"]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out what you can do to ",["prepare for and respond to extreme weather and natural hazards","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/tropical-cyclones"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Earthquakes"]},{"k":"p","s":["Earthquakes are a risk in Tajikistan, particularly the east in the Gorno-Badakhshan Autonomous Region. Avalanches and landslides caused by earthquakes often block roads in the spring and early summer."]},{"k":"p","s":["Learn earthquake safety procedures and follow the advice of the local authorities. The US Federal Emergency Management Agency website has advice about ",["what to do before, during and after an earthquake","https://www.ready.gov/earthquakes"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Flooding"]},{"k":"p","s":["In late spring and summer, there can be seasonal flooding and mudslides caused by melting glaciers. Take care, follow local advice and be aware that conditions can change suddenly."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Snow"]},{"k":"p","s":["Heavy snowfall in winter can cause delays and cancellations at airports and disrupt travel, particularly in mountainous regions where there’s an increased risk of avalanches. Take local advice on road conditions during or following severe weather."]},{"k":"h","s":["Regional risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["This section has safety advice for regions of Tajikistan. It only covers regions where FCDO has specific advice."]},{"k":"p","s":["You should also read ",["FCDO’s overall travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/tajikistan"]," and ",["safety and security advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/tajikistan/safety-and-security"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Border crossings"]},{"k":"p","s":["Tajikistan’s borders with neighbouring countries can close without notice and some borders may not be open to foreign travellers."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check with the Tajikistan authorities before you travel to see which crossings are open."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Tajikistan-Kyrgyzstan border"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a history of border clashes in this area, and the security situation can change at short notice. There have been no further clashes since the border agreement in 2025. However, unexploded landmines and weapons continue to pose a serious risk. Border areas may be subject to sudden restrictions on movement and a heightened security presence. You should exercise caution if travelling near the Kyrgyzstan–Tajikistan border, check local conditions before travel, and follow the advice of the local authorities."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Tajikistan-Afghanistan border"]},{"k":"p","s":["In November 2025, 5 Chinese nationals were killed in 2 separate cross-border attacks launched from Afghanistan in the Shamsiddin Shohon (Khatlon) and Darvoz (GBAO) regions. On 13 August 2026, a local resident was killed by a stray bullet in Darvoz during armed clashes along the border of Afghanistan’s Badakhshan Province."]},{"k":"p","s":["Armed clashes involving terrorist or criminal groups may occur without notice close to the Tajikistan border in Afghanistan’s Badakhshan region. Armed groups have previously conducted cross-border incursions from Afghanistan. You should stay alert in border regions and follow the instructions of local authorities. Do not walk off-road – there are both marked and unmarked minefields."]},{"k":"h","s":["Gorno-Badakhshan Autonomous Region"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a risk of civil unrest in Khorog and other towns in the Gorno-Badakhshan Autonomous Region (GBAO). There were serious disturbances in 2021 and there have been violent clashes in and around Khorog since 2022 with casualties. There is an increased security presence. Some roads in Khorog, Rushan and other parts of Gorno-Badakhshan Autonomous Region are temporarily closed. The security situation can change at short notice, with the possibility of further unrest."]},{"k":"p","s":["Border Guard patrols may ask to see your passport and GBAO permit when you travel in GBAO, particularly in areas close to the border with Afghanistan"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re travelling in the region, be alert in public places and check for security announcements by the local authorities."]},{"k":"h","s":["Tavildara Region"]},{"k":"p","s":["Take local advice in the Tavildara Region of central Tajikistan, as there are minefields dating from the civil war in the mountains."]},{"k":"p","s":["Medical and rescue facilities are unreliable where they exist at all."]},{"k":"h","s":["Health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Before you travel check that:"]},{"k":"li","s":["your destination can provide the healthcare you may need"]},{"k":"li","s":["you have ",["appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"]," for local treatment or unexpected medical evacuation"]},{"k":"p","s":["This is particularly important if you have a health condition or are pregnant."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency medical number"]},{"k":"p","s":["Call 03 (or 103 from a mobile phone) and ask for an ambulance. The operator will likely only speak Tajik and Russian."]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your insurance company quickly if you’re referred to a medical facility for treatment."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine recommendations and health risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["At least 8 weeks before your trip:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check the latest ",["vaccine recommendations for Tajikistan","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/219/tajikistan#Vaccine_Recommendations"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see where to get vaccines and whether you have to pay on the ",["NHS travel vaccinations page","https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/travel-vaccinations/"]]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["what health risks you’ll face in Tajikistan","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/219/tajikistan"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Altitude sickness is a risk in parts of Tajikistan. Read more about ",["altitude sickness on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/26/altitude-illness"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Air quality"]},{"k":"p","s":["Tajikistan, particularly Dushanbe and Khatlon region, often suffers from poor air quality, particularly during dust storms. Try to minimise your exposure to outside air by staying in an air-conditioned indoor place as much as possible, with windows and doors closed and well sealed."]},{"k":"p","s":["Wash all fruit, vegetables and other foods, which might have been exposed. Regularly damp-dust all indoor surfaces, washing your hands afterwards. Monitor local reports and weather forecasts for the latest information and advice."]},{"k":"h","s":["Medication"]},{"k":"p","s":["The legal status and regulation of some medicines prescribed or bought in the UK can be different in other countries."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["best practice when travelling with medicines on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/43/medicines-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Basic medicines including painkillers are available without a prescription. Phone a Tajik pharmacy in advance to check if your UK prescription will be accepted. You may need to get your UK prescription translated into Russian or Tajik. You can get a translation in Tajikistan– ",["find an interpreter or translator","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/translators-interpreters?country=Tajikistan"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Some prescription medications are not widely available. Medications often come under different brand names and Western brand name drugs may be counterfeit, so ask for the drug’s generic name. If your medication is not available, you may be able to get it couriered from a third country, though this could take time."]},{"k":"p","s":["You may need to pay cash for medication"]},{"k":"h","s":["Healthcare in Tajikistan"]},{"k":"p","s":["The quality of medical care in Tajikistan is generally poor. Most medical facilities are badly equipped and unhygienic, with a limited supply of drugs. Medical facilities outside Dushanbe are quite basic and, in some locations, almost non-existent. There is no guarantee that equipment will have been properly sterilised, especially in rural hospitals. There is no reciprocal healthcare agreement between the UK and Tajikistan"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has a ",["list of medical providers in Tajikistan","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/tajikistan-list-of-medical-facilities"]," where some staff will speak English."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travel and mental health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["FCDO guidance on travel and mental health","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-advice-for-people-with-mental-health-issues"],". There is also ",["mental health guidance on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/85/travelling-with-mental-health-conditions"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Getting help"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) cannot provide tailored advice for individual trips. Read this travel advice and carry out your own research before deciding whether to travel."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency services in Tajikistan"]},{"k":"p","s":["Emergency services do not speak English."]},{"k":"p","s":["Ambulance: 03 (103 from mobile phone)"]},{"k":"p","s":["Fire: 01 (101 from mobile phone)"]},{"k":"p","s":["Police: 02 (102 from mobile phone)"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contact your travel provider and insurer"]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your travel provider and your insurer if you are involved in a serious incident or emergency abroad. They will tell you if they can help and what you need to do."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Refunds and changes to travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["For refunds or changes to travel, contact your travel provider. You may also be able to make a claim through insurance. However, insurers usually require you to talk to your travel provider first."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["changing or cancelling travel plans","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice#changing-or-cancelling-travel-plans"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["where to get advice if you are in a dispute with a provider"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to access previous versions of travel advice to support a claim"]},{"k":"h","s":["Support from FCDO"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has guidance on staying safe and what to do if you need help or support abroad, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["finding English-speaking ",["lawyers","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/lawyers?country=Tajikistan"],", ",["funeral directors","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/funeral-directors?country=Tajikistan"]," and ",["translators and interpreters","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/translators-interpreters?country=Tajikistan"]," in Tajikistan"]},{"k":"li","s":["dealing with a ",["death in Tajikistan","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/tajikistan-bereavement-death-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["being ",["arrested or imprisoned in Tajikistan","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/tajikistan-prisoner-pack"]]},{"k":"li","s":["getting help if you’re a ",["victim of crime","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/victim-of-crime-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["what to do if you’re ",["in hospital","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/in-hospital-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["if you’re ",["affected by a crisis","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"],", such as a terrorist attack"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contacting FCDO"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help abroad"]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["how to get help from the UK government abroad","https://www.contact.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/posts/tajikistan/british-embassy-dushanbe"]," including in an emergency."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help in the UK"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can call FCDO in London if you need urgent help because something has happened to a friend or relative abroad."]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 020 7008 5000 (24 hours)"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Find out about call charges","https://www.gov.uk/call-charges"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/tajikistan/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]}],"chars":29620,"change":"New information about terrorism and armed clashes near the Tajikistan-Afghanistan border ('Safety and security' and ‘Regional risks’ pages)."}};
